<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC
  "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN"
  "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>
A derivation declares the same package in <code>propagatedBuildInputs</code>
and in <code>checkInputs</code> or <code>nativeCheckInputs</code>.
</p>
<p>
In nixpkgs, everything from <code>propagatedBuildInputs</code> is already
available during the check phase, so repeating the same package in a check-only
input list is redundant.
</p>
<p>
This query is intentionally syntactic: it only checks direct list literals on
both attributes. Dynamically constructed lists are ignored.
</p>
</overview>

<recommendation>
<p>
Keep runtime dependencies in <code>propagatedBuildInputs</code> and list only
extra test-only dependencies in <code>checkInputs</code> or
<code>nativeCheckInputs</code>. Remove any package that appears in both places.
</p>
</recommendation>

<example>
<p>Problematic — <code>pytest</code> is listed twice:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, pytest, requests }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  propagatedBuildInputs = [ requests pytest ];
  checkInputs = [ pytest ];
}
</sample>
<p>Recommended — keep <code>pytest</code> only where it is needed:</p>
<sample language="nix">
{ stdenv, requests, pytest }:
stdenv.mkDerivation {
  pname = "demo";
  version = "1.0";
  propagatedBuildInputs = [ requests ];
  checkInputs = [ pytest ];
}
</sample>
</example>

<references>
<li>
<a href="https://github.com/jtojnar/nixpkgs-hammering/blob/main/explanations/duplicate-check-inputs.md">
<code>nixpkgs-hammering</code> explanation: <code>duplicate-check-inputs</code></a>
</li>
</references>
</qhelp>
